speechtext:
Whereas there exists in Canada an acute unemployment situation;
And whereas, it is desirable that as many as possible be absorbed into the useful industrial life of the dominon;
Therefore be it resolved, that, in the opinion pf this house, the government he requested to immediately introduce legislation granting adequate retiring allowances to all citizens over sixty years of age, thereby giving an opportunity to large numbers now unemployed to be reabsorbed into useful productive activity.
He said: As I rise this afternoon to propose this motion I cannot help being reminded of the fact that it is just about ten years ago that the house passed the existing old age pensions law. Even at this late date I would express my own appreciation and that of my colleague the hon. member for Winnipeg North Centre (Mr. Woodsworth) of what was done by the then government, many members of which are in the present cabinet, and thank them for the kind and courteous reception we were given in 1926. I trust that on this occasion we shall receive the same sympathetic consideration as we got about ten years ago.
